  "_lark_msg": "Unsupported field type. (the refusing kinds)",
  "_verdict": "THREE FINDINGS. (1) THE KIT'S FIRST ENTRY BECOMES THE PRIMARY COLUMN: every kitted create read back with the array's first entry flagged is_primary and NO locale-named default column anywhere in the listing, while the name-only control got the locale-named primary. (2) THIS ROUTE'S KIND VOCABULARY IS NARROWER THAN POST .../fields's: ['Rating', 'Checkbox'] answer 1254012 and create NOTHING — no table, no columns — while ['Text', 'Number', 'DateTime', 'SingleSelect', 'Barcode', 'Currency', 'Progress'] land with their property intact. (3) tables/batch_create ACCEPTS a per-table `fields` array and IGNORES it: code 0, kit honoured = False — every table arrives with the locale-named default primary and none of the kit. Sent as a hand-written raw body, so the swallow is the SERVER's, not the library's.",
  "_note": "LD-336. Q1 asked whether the array's first entry BECOMES the primary or arrives beside the locale-named one Lark creates itself; the primary column per case was {\"A name only (the control)\": [\"多行文本\"], \"B one field: name + type\": [\"b\"], \"C one field + ui_type\": [\"c\"], \"D two fields\": [\"d1\"], \"E property WITHOUT ui_type\": [\"e\"]} — so it BECOMES it, and the older guess (a kit adds columns beside the default) is refuted. Q2 asked whether the two authoring routes share a vocabulary; they do not, which is why the shipped kit gate refuses the measured-refusing kinds LOCALLY and names create_field as the route that does author them. Case E is the R12 warning beside it: a `property` sent with NO `ui_type` is accepted and SILENTLY IGNORED — the column lands as the storage type's default kind — which is why the shipped builder never sends a property without the ui_type it belongs to. This list is what was MEASURED (9 kinds), not a claim about the whole enum.",
  "_transport": "larkdocio.common.transport.CredentialedRawHttpClient (urllib), paced 1.3 s — the RAW core, because the question is what the server does with a body",
  "_disposable": "one, harness-created; deleted in the harness finally, ledger-backed",
